    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "\u2705 **Bug fixed and verified!**\n\n**The issue:** The main `frai` program defines a `--ci` option at the top level. When running `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was consuming the `--ci` flag before passing arguments to the gate subcommand, so only `['init']` reached the gate handler instead of `['init', '--ci']`.\n\n**The fix:** I modified the gate command action in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 752-753) to extract all arguments from `process.argv` starting after the \"gate\" keyword:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n```\n\nThis ensures all flags like `--ci` are passed through to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n**Verification:** After rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, I tested the command and confirmed both files are now created:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713",
